# SMBPal repo hygiene — copy to .gitignore at the root of every SMBPal repo.
#
# D5 opens these repos once established, and we publish the FULL history rather than
# squashing or splitting repos (§11.3). That decision is only safe if nothing
# unpublishable ever lands, because a later delete does not remove it from history.

# --- Captured Samba config -------------------------------------------------
# SMBPal's job is generating smb.conf, so templates and fixtures are legitimate and are
# un-ignored below. What must never be committed is a real one lifted off a machine:
# it carries hostnames, absolute paths, usernames and sometimes credentials.
smb.conf
smb.conf.*
*.smb.conf
!*.smb.conf.in
!tests/fixtures/*.smb.conf.example

# --- Signing and notarization (§11.3, line 654: "belong in no repository") --
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
AuthKey_*.p8

# --- Credentials -----------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.*
credentials.*
*.keychain
*.keychain-db

# ...but never a source file. `credentials.*` matched `smbpal/mounts/credentials.py`
# — a module, not a secret — and swallowed it for ten days from 20 August 2026.
# Nothing noticed, because both machines had it another way: the Mac wrote it,
# and the Pi receives the tree by rsync, which has never heard of this file. A
# clone of this repository could not import the daemon, the CLI or the GUI, and
# §11.3 was going to publish that. Found by the first CI run there has ever been.
!credentials.py
!secrets.py

# --- Build and interpreter artifacts ---------------------------------------
# Nothing here is unpublishable, but §11.3 publishes full history and a repo
# carrying __pycache__ from three machines is history nobody wants to read.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Debian build artefacts ------------------------------------------------
# `debian` is a symlink to `packaging/debian`, so debhelper writes its working
# files *inside the repository* rather than beside it. §11.3 publishes full
# history, and a history carrying build detritus from three machines is
# history nobody wants to read.
packaging/debian/.debhelper/
packaging/debian/smbpal/
packaging/debian/files
packaging/debian/debhelper-build-stamp
packaging/debian/*.substvars
packaging/debian/*.debhelper
packaging/debian/*.debhelper.log
*.deb
*.buildinfo
*.changes

# --- Platform noise --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
